{"created": "2026-10-15T04:00:29.066300+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-15T04:00:29.475789+00:00", "id": 23383961, "conceptrecid": "23383960", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23383961", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23383960", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23383961", "metadata": {"title": "Nonmonotone Argument and Radial Angle of a Support Slit", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23383961", "publication_date": "2026-10-14", "description": "<p>Every global maximizer of the real part of a2+i*10^-24(a4-3a3) in the normalized schlicht class omits a slit with nonmonotone continuous argument and nonmonotone signed and ordinary unsigned radial angles. This gives negative answers to the two questions recorded as Hayman-Lingham Problem 6.72. Compactness provides genuine extremizers, the area theorem bounds the actual slit tip, and a controlled Schiffer natural coordinate identifies a subarc of the actual omitted slit. No explicit maximizing function or uniqueness is required.</p><p>The research note credits classical support-slit geometry, Schiffer methods and the Friedland-Schiffer coefficient/control framework. The accompanying package contains manuscript source, immutable authored input, independent analytic and quantitative derivations, exact rational and directed interval checks, and a bounded primary-source priority audit. Complete comparisons include Zemyan (2003, 2005, 2007), Duren-Leung-Schiffer (1983), Zhang-Ma (1991), Brickman (1984), and Goh (1992, 1994). The later Duren commentary (2013 online/2014 print) and Hibschweiler (1995) could not be inspected. Priority therefore cannot be fully cleared. These limitations and other uninspected leads are disclosed; no historical-first priority or continued open status in 2026 is asserted. Finite controls supplement the uniform analytic proofs and are not formal certification of the classical inputs.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in development, writing, reproduction and adversarial verification. This is an unrefereed preprint with internal AI adversarial reviews; it has not received human peer review.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["univalent functions", "support points", "Schiffer differential", "omitted slit", "nonmonotone argument", "radial angle", "counterexample", "exact rational verification"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/563", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.07200v2", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/BF02566218", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5186/aasfm.1971.489", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1090/S0002-9947-1985-0766220-8", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/BF02813301", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1080/02781070310001599359", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/BF03321083", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1080/17476930601065169", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1080/17476938308814018", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1016/0022-247X(91)90330-3", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1090/S0002-9939-1984-0759655-5", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1090/S0002-9939-1994-1197537-4", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1080/17476939208814600", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/978-1-4614-7949-9_22", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://www.math.uh.edu/~hjm/vol21-1.html", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version"